en the people around  you don't accept what you have when you  want to take something in a new  direction i could have done something  else i could have done something easier  if i just did a book about jack ma right  in his real  success that would be easier to pick up  than this  which i talk about on the channel but  it's not the main thesis of the channel  but that's what i want to make and  that's what i'm going to make whether  it's i get a publisher or we're going to  you know create it myself it's going to  be birthed into existence because i  decided so  and just taking that mindset and  approach you have to if you love the  thing if you're doing something  different  then you have to keep going when people  say that i don't want to pick it up that  it sucks that it's stupid that  you're maybe it's even a great idea but  you're not the person who's gonna do it  right you have to keep going so i get  rejecting all the time  um most recently on the book that's a  big thing  and i'm proud that we got our publisher  at least and we're getting it out and  we're doing the tour and  that's it it's amazing even even the  tour i wanted to start in january for  the tour right january 16th we're gonna  be in cleveland  it's official the book's not coming out  until march  something 23rd 17th something like that  and like you want you to hold off on the  tour until the book's ready like no no  we're going  that was decided tour's happening we're  gonna start a tour and we'll do  pre-orders  until until the book is out and then we  can hand it out to people at the end and  mail it out to the people  who came before right like you decide  and you make stuff happen  and people will constantly have their  own agenda and own ideas for what you  should do with your life  you need to own what you want to do with  your life and then will it into  existence  so how do you do it i'm going to give  you a three-step process that i think  will help step number one is tie your  self-worth to the effort not the outcome  this is this  is this is one of the biggest things  that holds entrepreneurs back  you tie your self-worth to the result to  the outcome  you're great because a publisher says  yes right if that's why  if that's how i tied myself worth i'm  only good  if i get a million subscribers i'm only  good  if a publisher says yes no no i'm  awesome i wrote an amazing book this  book is fire  it's life-changing for people and evan  carmichael is awesome for writing it  whether a publisher loves it or not  right  because if you take that mindset right  take that substitute your name and your  project in that sentence you take that  mindset and you start to apply it  and you believe you're awesome for the  work that you're creating that allows  you  the strength the fortitude the  persistence to keep going  right it doesn't mean never listen to  feedback if a publisher said like  tweak it like this and tweak it like  that and maybe we could do a deal you  listen to it you're open you have to  match what you love with  what the demand is but if you felt  like you're insanely proud of your  effort for everything you create  you will go off and create amazing  things if you constantly tie your  self-worth to whether somebody likes it  or not  you're going to lose for life because  you're tying yourself forward to people  who have a lower standard than you  it doesn't make sense you're never going  to win you want to be creative  disruptive  a game-changing badass world-changing  entrepreneur like you have to  bet on yourself on your ideas when  people think you're crazy i look at the  thumbnails that i've done on my on my  youtube channel  i split test maybe more than anybody on  youtube we've done almost 1500 different  split tests on titles and thumbnails  and every time i go through it every  time i finish a round of another 10  different  variations new ideas right i'm always  trying to beat my best  i feel amazing like man i just made this  this is i love it i think this is going  to be the thing i always think it's  going to win  i don't make something that i think is  gonna lose i think it's gonna win  but most of the time it loses most of  the time it loses  and when it loses like ah crap  right now what just go back to what  we're doing that's not acceptable we got  to keep going keep building  but i feel great that i tried i'm still  proud of the effort even though  all of the things i created for those  sample thumbnails they're all in the  garbage i must have  [Music]  thousands thousands of thumbnails that  didn't even get to testing  that i'm still proud that i made that  just never saw  the light of day so being proud of your  effort  like what are you doing right now that  you're proud of your effort on whether  you win the race or not  you tried your hardest because if every  day you wake up and you try your hardest  you're going to win way more races than  you thought possible but if all you're  focused on is winning that one race  and you lose and then you quit and give  up you're losing on life  tie your self-worth to the effort not  the outcome  step number two is find another way  there's always another way right there's  always another way  this is the entrepreneur mindset it's  not about the resources it's about how  resourceful you are right there's  always another way what's the other way  for the book the other way is go find  another publisher go find another  publisher go find another publisher or  self-publish it myself or turn it into a  youtube video that  is three hours long and i read the whole  thing i don't know there's always  another way  there's always another way don't stop at  the first no or the second no or the  80th no  there is always another way  just adopt it if you love this thing  because here's here's what's gonna  happen if you love it  if you love it you know you have to  create this thing it's inside you you  love it  and you stop you're gonna regret it your  whole life you're gonna regret that you  didn't push a little bit harder a little  bit more  try another angle tap into your genius  but if you keep going even though you  haven't got a yes yet even though you  haven't got a win yet  but you love it you have to keep going  you have to keep going so you don't  regret the rest of your entire life  right there's always another way just  embody it  embrace it believe it the thing that you  want to do  is genius trust it keep going and find  another way and step number three is  what i call the tom bill you list  and this is not something i subscribe to  but works up for other people  like tom and so i wanted to share it for  you as an option tom's talked a lot  about  how he keeps a list so he's got a list  of people who doubted him  who told him he was never gonna make it  uh who told them that he was stupid or  an idiot or just  you know never gonna make it they didn't  believe in him insulted him either rude  or just said no to him and he wrote  their names down on the list and he's  got this list where there's actually a  like a  a printed list or just a list in his  head um and anytime he feels like he  doesn't want to get out of bed  anytime he's had a particularly bad day  then he reminds himself of the list  and he starts thinking about the people  and as if i don't get out of bed and go  do this thing  i'm that person is right and it fuels  him to get off and go off and do the  thing  right now you don't want to live in  negativity you  you don't want to only do the thing  because your uncle joe says you're an  idiot and you're never going to do it  right uncle joe not believing in you  can't be the motivation and  the sole reason for you going off but in  moments of acute  pain right you're you're 80 90 driven by  the positive and the inspiring  and the mission and the change that  you're trying to create and then the  final 10 and 20  when you need just that little extra  kick going to the dark side and saying  i'm going to prove uncle joe ron or  whoever  screwed you over and doesn't believe in  you i don't go there  that doesn't motivate me but it does for  highly successful entrepreneurs like tom  and other people so i wanted to give you  the option  try out the tom bill you list the next  time you are feeling low  energy and not following through and you  got rejected  use those names to propel you forward  and say  i am going to do it to prove you wrong  this is why it's so important that you  love what you do success is painful  it's a lot of work a lot of stress a lot  of failure  a lot of rejection but the thing that  gets you through it  is you love what you do you love the  process you love the work  you love the growth if you don't love  the work you do you will give up because  it will just become too painful to keep  going  so at the whole foods this morning when  i went to go get my bulletproof coffee  i ran into a friend of mine an  entrepreneur friend of mine who i told  about my tour  in december before i left and she was  super excited and i hadn't connected  with her since i got back  i went on this three month 90 day 23  city tour  across the u.s and it was amazing  happened since to meet her at the whole  foods  this morning and she said how's the tour  what was the best part of it  and i said break in my neck two-thirds  of the way through i broke my neck  i broke my neck in two spots i  compressed my spine i had a concussion  had to get staples in my head  all of it she said breaking your neck  that's the best part of your torah  that's a really positive outlook like  it's not just a positive outlook it's  the best  like it actually was the best part  because it really got the test like why  this sounds crazy but this is it this is  this is the process this is the mindset  shift  i want you guys to make that you do  difficult things  you love difficult things you don't want  it to be easy easy means you're inside  your comfort zone  easy means you're not pushing up against  any barriers you don't want to be easy  stop getting these easy small tiny wings  that you can snack on  you do difficult things you love taking  on amazing huge things that's who you  are  that's what you do and this was a chance  for me to grow  and help cement that for myself  rejection is part of life as an  entrepreneur  you are going to get rejected over and  over and over and over again it's just  part of being an entrepreneur and being  a business  the first thing you put out won't be  very good people will hate on it people  give some constructive criticism  as well people will say no because they  don't know you trust you like you  and so you won't get those first deals  it takes a lot of time to build up a  business and make it successful and even  when you've gotten to that point where  you're feeling happy and you're bringing  on a team and  building the business you're still going  to get rejected constantly it's just  part of life as an entrepreneur so if  you can't handle that  it's going to be a really hard road for  you to be an entrepreneur  i think the way to get through rejection  there's two ways to do it one is use  rejection as fuel  kind of like what jack ma did like i got  rejected 10 times by harvard one day i'm  gonna go teach  there right when they're gonna go speak  there to use that as she was like you  turned me down  i'm gonna show you i'm gonna beat it i'm  gonna  come back and be the teacher there right  you turn me down for this deal i'm gonna  go get a deal 10 times as big  right so that's one you can easily you  can use rejection as fuel to help you go  off and do something  bigger and motivation to i'm going to  prove them wrong  the second way is just to forget about  it just  get used to it that's more what i do i  don't really use rejection as fuel  doesn't really bother me when somebody  turns me down or when a new  series doesn't work i was trying to  think when i was preparing for this 